{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/169241-overwhelmed","id":169241,"title":"Overwhelmed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-14T14:06:29-07:00","id":169241,"title":"Overwhelmed","content":"I've never run a full on nWoD chronicle before and i would like to run Demon but the vast amount of rules and information seem overwhelming (new world of darkness rulebook, demon). Ive only run simpler games like Savage Worlds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T15:01:11-07:00","id":169286,"title":"","content":"Well.. the first thing you need to remember - don't overstress the rules. If you mess something up - so be it, you'll play it correct the next time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:31:04-07:00","id":169391,"title":"","content":"Having run both, I don't think SW is any simpler, but it might be because I'm so much more familiar with NWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T20:06:49-07:00","id":169424,"title":"","content":"If you're looking to introduce the game a little bit at a time, I'd recommend using the <i>Ready-Made Characters</i> and only paying attention to the powers they've got on their sheets. Generally, you can avoid any rule in nWoD until you're ready to introduce it, without breaking things. So you might play through with just basic resolution and combat, then start using powers the next session. Then wait until you're comfortable with that to start tracking experience and therefore Conditions. Then play with that until you're ready for Cover, and so on.<br /> <br /> You can basically pick the stuff you like best or find easiest to understand and go along with that until you're ready to add more.<br /> <br /> (You can also simplify things by running a human-only game for a while, but I'm assuming since you posted in this forum that <i>Demon</i> is the setting you're more interested in.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 06-15-2014, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T20:57:21-07:00","id":169457,"title":"","content":"Most important thing is to make it clear to your players that your familiarity with the rules is shaky, and that while you'll do your best, you'd appreciate their help. I'm guessing they've never played it either? If not, then that's ok, mistakes will inevitably be made, but you'll all learn together, and if you're up-front about your flawed knowledge, they'll be pretty forgiving as long as you seem to be making an effort.<br /> <br /> First, get to know the basic, underlying system. Don't worry about powers and conditions too much at this point. Just go over the sequences for combat (Initiative, attacking, damage, etc), maybe even run one or two practise combats with someone else if you can, as well as social combat, Cover and suchforth. The very basics. How do you resolve something your character wants to do? Thankfully, these are pretty straightforward with nWoD.<br /> <br /> Once you've got those more-or-less down, try eyeballing some of the Merits, and figure out how each of them fall within the general ruleset you learned earlier. Powers too, if you're feeling enthusiastic. Don't try to memorise all of them: I know people that do that, and I guess it works for them, but I generally take a bit of a functionalist view.<br /> <br /> As long as you've got those more-or-less sorted, you should be ok. You'll make mistakes, but that's inevitable no matter how well you know the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}